Gaokao-Bench Changelog
======================

Versioning
----------
- Engine versions track the harness, scorer, CLI, packaging, and release tools.
- Dataset versions track questions, answers, points, assets, and manifest policy.
- A published result must record both versions plus the dataset and protocol hashes.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.4 / Dataset 0.0.4

- Close dataset 0.0.4 with `audited_passed` statuses for every answer, question,
  point row, asset, review event, and owner signoff. The protocol is explicitly
  `owner_attested_single_review`; independent review is marked not applicable,
  not claimed and not left pending. The public manifest uses the same top-level
  `status: audited_passed`; `package_profile: public-data` identifies the
  sanitized distribution format.
- Enforce one canonical metric for new datasets:
  `scoring.primary_metric=score.weighted_points`, matching the Benchmark Spec.
  The legacy `0.0.1`/`0.0.3` packages remain readable through their historical
  adapter and immutable manifests.
- Split `retrospective_public_2025` from the required `post_cutoff_live` track.
  Public 2025 questions cannot be presented as held-out or fresh.
- Canonical runs default to 5 repeats, 900-second timeout, 32768 output tokens,
  provider pinning, disabled fallbacks, seed/fingerprint verification, bootstrap
  confidence intervals, and per-question flip rates. `reasoning_budget=8192` is
  a separate constrained track; the engine, not only the CLI, withholds canonical
  status when timeout, output budget, or reasoning constraints do not match.
- Treat the four-question visual slice as diagnostic-only; standalone visual
  ranking requires at least 30 questions.
- Record Shanghai Q11 rounding precision and mark `12.57`/`12.59` as borderline
  candidates while keeping only the correctly rounded value correct.
- Publish `RELEASE_CARD.json`, `COMPATIBILITY.md`, audit evidence, and the same
  metric/version matrix in the source and Hugging Face packages.
- Separate dataset publication from score publication: a missing clean model run
  blocks a public model score or leaderboard entry, but no longer blocks the
  immutable, owner-attested question package itself.
- Bind public owner attestations to the sanitized public projection hashes, make
  release gates resolve both source-root and `audit/` evidence layouts, and
  validate content-lineage hashes against the immutable package.
- Correct release diagrams that still described a two-reviewer process for the
  single-owner-attested 0.0.4 dataset.
- Update engine defaults, CLI documentation, release tooling, and tests to the
  0.1.4 / 0.0.4 pair.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.2 / Dataset 0.0.3

- License dataset 0.0.3 as a whole under CC BY 4.0, including question text,
  answers, figures, selection, schema, and scoring metadata; the code and
  harness remain Apache-2.0.
- Publish Hugging Face dataset metadata with license cc-by-4.0 and retain source
  attribution in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- Keep public_ranking_allowed=true with attribution and exact revision pinning.
- Treat public redistribution as cleared with attribution for 0.0.3 and later.
- Remove redundant licensing prose from README; authoritative terms remain in
  LICENSE-DATA and the dataset manifest.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.1 / Dataset 0.0.2

- Dataset 0.0.2 is a metadata-only update to 0.0.1. Questions, answers, points,
  and figure crops are unchanged.
- Set public_ranking_allowed=true for dataset 0.0.2. Third parties may publish
  leaderboards, comparative rankings, and model evaluation results when they cite
  the exact dataset revision and evaluation protocol.
- Keep exam_material_license=NOASSERTION. Permission to rank model results does
  not relicense the underlying exam text, figures, or third-party material.
- Dataset 0.0.1 remains immutable and keeps its historical
  public_ranking_allowed=false manifest.
- Fix the scoring formula so the metric identifier renders correctly in KaTeX.
- Remove the engine release tip from README; release history is maintained here.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.0 / Dataset 0.0.1

- Split the subject-neutral Engine from versioned Benchmark Specs and immutable
  data packages.
- Add scoped point-weighted metrics, text/vision slices, provider routing records,
  failure usage accounting, progress events, resume, and retry-failed.
- Fix set-builder interval false negatives in the deterministic scorer.
- Add the all-subject construction, validator, evidence-level, and versioning
  architecture in ARCHITECTURE.md.

2026-11-09
----------
Dataset 0.0.1

- Publish the 2025 Gaokao Mathematics objective baseline: five papers, 74 scored
  questions, 353 official points, and four figure-required questions.
- Add deterministic all-or-nothing scoring, text and vision profiles, gold/empty/
  malformed examples, and immutable file hashes.
